course: dictionary
lesson: 11090
title: Whale: an animal and a fun time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A whale is a very large animal that lives in the sea. It looks like a fish, but it is a mammal, so it breathes air through a blowhole. The context helps you see this: «A whale calf is born tail first under water, and its mother helps it up for its first breath.» A calf is a baby whale, and it needs air just like you do.
explain: Whale has a second meaning, used in a phrase. «We had a whale of a time at the beach.» This does not mean you saw an animal. It means a really great, fun time. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about the sea, or about having fun?
explain: Size clues help too. «The blue whale, up to about 30 metres long, is heavier than any dinosaur.» Words like heavier and biggest tell you the whale is huge. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A whale is a mammal: it breathes air, is warm-blooded and feeds its babies milk.
fact: The blue whale is the largest animal that has ever lived, up to about 30 metres long.
fact: A baby whale is called a calf.
fact: «A whale of a time» means a really great, fun time.
fact: Humpback whales have the longest flippers of any whale, about a third of their body length.
exercise: What is a whale calf? | A kind of seaweed | A type of small fish | A young shark | *A baby whale
exercise: In «We had a whale of a time at the fair», what does whale of a time mean? | A time spent looking at whales | A cold and wet time | *A really great, fun time | A very long time
exercise: Whales are mammals. Which of these shows it? | It lays eggs in the sand | *It breathes air through a blowhole | It breathes water through gills | It has scales all over its body
test: «Humpbacks have the longest flippers of any whale.» Which whale has the longest flippers? | Killer whale | Blue whale | Megalodon | *Humpback whale
test: What do whale mothers feed their babies? | Fish | Krill | *Milk | Seaweed
exam: Which sentence uses whale to mean the animal? | My whale-themed bag is red | *The whale swam up to the surface to breathe air | We had a whale of a time at the fair | The whale party was loud and fun
